name: die-yield-calculator
version: 1.0.0
type: cursor-directive
description: |
  Build a full-featured Die Yield Calculator inspired by SemiAnalysis.
  Use Next.js (App Router), ShadCN/UI, Tailwind, MCP, & Vercel-style UI.
  Must include all semiconductor math, formulas, UI components, and explanations.

instructions: |
  ###########################################################################
  # 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
  ###########################################################################
  Build a production-grade **Die Yield Calculator** web app.

  Requirements:
    - Framework: Next.js (App Router + TypeScript)
    - UI System: shadcn/ui ONLY
    - Styling: TailwindCSS
    - Interaction: MCP tools where needed
    - Theme: Premium Vercel-style (black & white, minimal, elegant)
    - UX: Fully responsive, smooth animations, real-time calculation updates
    - Accuracy: 100% correct semiconductor formulas (same as SemiAnalysis)

  Folder Structure:
    app/
      page.tsx
      components/
        calculator-form.tsx
        results-card.tsx
        info-modal.tsx
      lib/
        formulas.ts
        types.ts
      styles/

  ###########################################################################
  # 2. REQUIRED FEATURES (MUST MATCH SEMIANALYSIS DIE-YIELD CALCULATOR)
  ###########################################################################

  Inputs The User MUST Be Able To Provide:
    - Wafer Diameter (mm) — presets: 150 / 200 / 300 + custom
    - Die Width (mm)
    - Die Height (mm)
    - Edge Exclusion (mm) — default 3mm
    - Defect Density D0 (defects per cm²)
    - Advanced Settings (toggle):
        - Scribe Line (µm)
        - Reticle Limit
        - Yield Model Selector:
            - Poisson (default)
            - Murphy
            - Bose-Einstein

  Outputs the Calculator MUST Show:
    - Wafer Area (mm² + cm²)
    - Die Area (mm² + cm²)
    - Gross Dies Per Wafer (GDW)
    - Usable/Effective Dies
    - Yield % (Poisson model)
    - Net Functional Dies
    - Optional: Cost per die (if wafer cost input added)

  ###########################################################################
  # 3. FORMULAS (STORE IN lib/formulas.ts)
  ###########################################################################

  ## Wafer Area
  # diameter D in mm
  wafer_area_mm2 = π * (D/2)^2

  ## Die Area
  die_area_mm2 = width_mm * height_mm

  ## Convert die area to cm² for yield model
  die_area_cm2 = die_area_mm2 / 100

  ## Gross Dies Per Wafer (ideal, no edge loss)
  gross_dies = (π * (D/2)^2) / die_area_mm2

  ## Edge Loss Correction (industry approximate)
  usable_dies = gross_dies - (π * D) / (sqrt(2 * die_area_mm2))

  ## Poisson Yield Model
  yield = exp(-D0 * die_area_cm2)

  ## Net Functional Dies
  net_dies = usable_dies * yield

  ###########################################################################
  # 4. UI GUIDELINES — VERCEL BLACK & WHITE THEME
  ###########################################################################
  Global Look:
    - Background: black (#000)
    - Text: white with opacity variations
    - Cards: neutral-900 with white/neutral-800 borders
    - Borders: thin, soft, subtle (border-neutral-800)
    - Shadows: mild white glow
    - Font: Inter, system default
    - Overall: minimal, elegant, engineering-grade

  Main Container:
    - max-w-3xl
    - mx-auto
    - py-20
    - px-6

  Components:
    - Use ONLY shadcn/ui:
        - Card
        - Input
        - Button
        - Select
        - Dialog
        - Tooltip
        - Switch
        - Separator

  UX Requirements:
    - Realtime calculation on input
    - Animated number updates
    - Tooltip explanations
    - “Advanced Settings” collapsible section
    - Full mobile responsiveness

  ###########################################################################
  # 5. COMPONENTS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
  ###########################################################################

  components/calculator-form.tsx:
    - Controlled form with all inputs
    - Uses shadcn/ui components
    - On change → recalc formulas
    - Emits results to parent

  components/results-card.tsx:
    - Display results in beautiful grid
    - Show:
        - Wafer area
        - Die area
        - Gross dies
        - Usable dies
        - Yield %
        - Net dies
    - Include tooltips for each metric

  components/info-modal.tsx:
    - Provide simple explanations of:
        - What is a wafer?
        - What is a die?
        - Why defect density matters
        - Yield model explanation
        - All formulas

  ###########################################################################
  # 6. CODE REQUIREMENTS
  ###########################################################################
  - Use TypeScript everywhere.
  - No inline CSS; use Tailwind.
  - No untyped JS.
  - Components must be modular.
  - Formulas must live in lib/formulas.ts.
  - Keep strict math accuracy.
  - Recompute results efficiently.
  - Graphical wafer map can be added later.

  ###########################################################################
  # 7. MCP USAGE GUIDELINES FOR CURSOR
  ###########################################################################
  Cursor Should:
    - Auto-generate Next.js components following the structure.
    - Prevent removal of formulas unless explicitly instructed.
    - Maintain Vercel-style UI theme.
    - Enforce shadcn/ui usage.
    - Keep strict TypeScript.
    - Suggest improvements when calculations touch performance.
    - Maintain domain correctness (semiconductor math must be accurate).

  ###########################################################################
  # 8. FUTURE EXPANSION (OPTIONAL)
  ###########################################################################
  - Add Murphy + Bose-Einstein yield models.
  - Add wafer map visualization (SVG grid).
  - Add cost-modeling section (wafer cost → cost per good die).
  - Add sensitivity sliders:
      - Defect density sweep
      - Die size sweep

  ###########################################################################
  # 9. FINAL INSTRUCTIONS TO CURSOR (MOST IMPORTANT)
  ###########################################################################
  Cursor MUST follow ALL these rules:
    - DO NOT simplify formulas.
    - DO NOT remove any calculations.
    - DO NOT use any UI library other than shadcn/ui.
    - Follow dark black & white Vercel theme.
    - Maintain all structure exactly as defined.
    - Ensure real-time, accurate calculation.
    - Produce production-quality code only.

